become a Thunderbird pilot it takes a  lot of practice and experience in order  to apply for the team we have about 10  years of fighter experience a minimum of  750 fighter hours hopefully you're one  of the three pots that are selected each  year for the team the mission of the  team is to represent the Air Force and  to do it with the pride precision the  professionalism that the Air Force shows  on a daily basis  ensure that we're all operating off the  same sheet of music we begin by  executing a mission brief so everybody  has no doubt in their mind about what's  about to happen we fly twice a day every  day just to make sure that you have the  consistency within the the flying skills  to be safe the communication with the  team is very very important so  everything that we say in a tone of our  voice see 109 right track typos out  contactor how we're saying things the  inflection that we use is what they're  keying off of to make sure that they're  in the correct position and they know  where they need to go at what time the  margin of error for flying these  airplanes this close to each other is  very small you're flying these aircraft  over moms and dads and sisters and  brothers and grandparents and so there  is no movement at all on safety  with any operations you're always going  to hit roadblocks all the pilots are  never perfectly a position but they're  always correcting to get back in  position but it's the immediate reaction  and getting back to step position which  allows for the safe execution of  information
 

